    {
      "id": "cobbi44",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Vice President"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Vice President occupies the second-highest constitutional office in India, ranking next to the President.",
        "The electoral college consists of members of both Houses of Parliament (both elected and nominated), excluding State Legislative Assemblies.",
        "Qualifications include being a citizen of India, completing 35 years of age, and being qualified for election as a member of the Rajya Sabha.",
        "Serves as ex-officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha and acts as President during vacancies for a maximum period of 6 months.",
        "Can be removed by a resolution passed by a majority of all the then members of Rajya Sabha (effective majority) and agreed to by Lok Sabha."
      ],
      "id": "olrbyat"
    },
